Sunday afternoon is pleasant.
Moti and I are in the park.
We are sitting on a bench.
I am eating a warm bun maska.
Moti smells the food.
He looks at me with big, sad eyes.
He wants my bun maska.
But I remember Asha's strict rule.
"No, Moti," I say firmly.
"You must not eat this," I tell him.
"Dogs must not eat human food."
"Sit down here," I tell him.
He sits down quietly.
I open my bag.
I take out his special treat.
"Take this," I say, and give it to him.
Moti happily eats his treat.
I quietly finish my bun maska.
